jobs.description:
**At Bayer, we believe work should matter. Every day, our teams push toward a future where "Health for all, Hunger for none" is within reach, and every role, from the lab to the field to the boardroom, helps us get there. We give people the ownership to shape outcomes, the support to grow through new skills and experiences, and a global community where different perspectives are valued. If you want your work to count and the room to become your best, you'll find it here.**



**We’re changing the way we work at Bayer, for higher productivity, faster innovation, and better results. We call it Dynamic Shared Ownership (DSO). Learn more about what DSO will mean for you in your new role here** **https://www.bayer.com/en/strategy/strategy**



**POSITION PURPOSE:**

As a Data Integration Engineer, you will support the reliable, secure and compliant operation of data integration services in a qualified environment. You will monitor services, handle requests and incidents, execute controlled changes, maintain documentation and support evidence for service qualification and audits. You will be part of a small, agile team that works in a DevOps spirit. Hierarchy is flat, so you will work directly with colleagues and take ownership early

A key part of the role is supporting the migration from the current environment to the new data integration environment. You will help prepare, test and execute migration activities, validate service readiness and data flows, and assist users and application teams during transition and stabilization.

You will also identify opportunities to automate recurring work, improve monitoring and support processes, and reduce manual effort. The role requires at least three years of relevant professional experience and good English communication skills, and offers a development path toward a more senior Data Integration Cloud Engineer position with increasing ownership of cloud platforms, integration pipelines, infrastructure automation and engineering practices.

**YOUR TASKS AND RESPONSIBILITIES:**

* Operate and support data integration services in a qualified environment, following approved procedures, controls and service management practices;
* Take increasing ownership of the support and quality of an established data integration service, keeping user needs and satisfaction in mind; proactively follow up on issues, communicate progress and coordinate improvements with relevant teams;
* Monitor platform availability, performance, capacity and data flows, and respond to alerts before they affect users or dependent applications;
* Triage and resolve incidents and service requests with structured troubleshooting, document findings and escalate complex issues;
* Execute routine operations such as service checks, access administration, configuration updates, deployments and patching under controlled change processes;
* Maintain accurate runbooks, operating procedures, support records, configuration information and qualification documentation;
* Collect operational evidence for audits, reviews and qualified-service controls, and support remediation of identified gaps;
* Support the migration to the new environment, including discovery, planning, dependency tracking, test preparation, execution and stabilization;
* Work with application teams and stakeholders to validate connectivity, access, data flows and acceptance criteria before and after migration;
* Automate repetitive or error-prone activities using scripting, APIs, CI/CD workflows or infrastructure automation;
* Improve monitoring, alerting, dashboards and support processes to increase reliability and shorten issue detection and recovery time;
* Support cloud-based data integration components and, with guidance, contribute to ingestion pipelines, platform configuration and deployment automation;
* Participate in problem management and root cause analysis, and implement preventive actions and service improvements;
